BRepClass3d: the solid classifier (BRepClass3d_SClassifier::Perform) takes
segments from the point to points of the faces one face after another
(BRepClass3d_SolidExplorer::Segment, OtherSegment) and drops a segment that
passes through an edge or a vertex or ends on a face's boundary; a face
whose surface holds the point gives none, and a face seen almost edge-on
gives only a weak one, which a later face holding the point discards. When
the faces ran out, the line was rejected and State() counted it as OUT. A
point in the plane of a far face of the shell, every other face of it seen
almost edge-on, was so found outside: BRepCheck_Solid took a point of one
cavity for lying outside the solid of another whose bottom face lies in its
plane (BRepCheck_SubshapeNotInShape), and the face-merged union of a
machine's 257 bodies was thrown away for the unmerged one (mitcad#1280). Now
the point is classified along fixed lines instead, from the point towards
32 points spread over the shape's box (an additive sequence of three
irrational steps, the same on every call), each past the box's farthest
corner, until one meets a face cleanly: a line that meets no face, touches
one or passes through an edge or a vertex is passed over as the segments
are. Only when none does is the line rejected, as before. Classifications
whose segments did not run out are unchanged.
